This distribution contains Spartacus, version 1.1.


LICENSE
=======

* See spartacus/LICENSE for license information.

* This distribution contains several files taken from the SML/NJ
   library. Note the corresponding copyright information in
   spartacus/src/smlnj-lib/COPYRIGHT.


INSTALLATION
============

* Spartacus is written in Standard ML. In order to build Spartacus you
   will need the MLton compiler, available from
   http://mlton.org/

* The MLton libraries are assumed to be installed in
   /usr/lib/mlton
   Adapt the first three lines of
   spartacus/src/spartacus.mlb to refer to the installation directory of
   the MLton libraries on your system.

* In order to build Spartacus, use

       make spartacus

   or alternatively

       mlton -codegen native -output spartacus src/spartacus.mlb

* Besides Spartacus, the distribution contains a formula translation
   tool (ftt), which can convert formulas of hybrid or description logics
   into other formats.

   If you want to install ftt, adapt
   spartacus/src/ftt.mlb in the same way as described above for
   spartacus/src/spartacus.mlb

   In order to build ftt, use

       make ftt

   or alternatively

       mlton -codegen native -output ftt src/ftt.mlb


RUNNING SPARTACUS
=================

* Running Spartacus without any options or with the option

       --help

   will display a list of available options.

* The directory spartacus/profiles contains configuration files
   that specify the configurations (1.conf, 2.conf) and ordering
   heuristics (ord?.conf) used in [1] (pp. 64-66, pp. 52-53).

   In order to run Spartacus with these configurations, run Spartacus
   with the option

       --profile=FILENAME

   where FILENAME is the name of the desired configuration file.


REFERENCES
==========

[1] Daniel N. Goetzmann. Spartacus: A Tableau Prover for Hybrid Logic,
     Master's Thesis, Saarland University, 2009. Available from
     http://ps.uni-sb.de/theses/goetzmann/goetzmann-mthesis.pdf
